[
  {
    "title": "Full repo names",
    "statement": "Give the full name of every repo, as text like `acme/api`.\n\nThe input has an `owner` and a `repos` array of names. Save the owner with `.owner as $owner` first. Then go through `.repos[]` and build the text: the owner, a `/`, then the repo name. Print each text as its own output.",
    "reference": ".owner as $owner | .repos[] | \"\\($owner)/\\(.)\"",
    "tests": [
      {
        "input": {
          "owner": "acme",
          "repos": [
            "api",
            "web",
            "docs"
          ]
        },
        "expected": "\"acme/api\"\n\"acme/web\"\n\"acme/docs\""
      },
      {
        "input": {
          "owner": "lab",
          "repos": [
            "tools"
          ]
        },
        "expected": "\"lab/tools\""
      },
      {
        "input": {
          "owner": "solo",
          "repos": []
        },
        "expected": ""
      },
      {
        "input": {
          "owner": "north",
          "repos": [
            "cli",
            "sdk"
          ]
        },
        "expected": "\"north/cli\"\n\"north/sdk\""
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Prices after discount",
    "statement": "Take the discount off the price of every item.\n\nThe input has a `discount` and an `items` array. Each item has a `name` and a `price`. Give an array of objects with `name` and `price`, where the new price is the old price minus the discount. Name the discount with `as $d` before you go into `.items`.",
    "reference": ".discount as $d | .items | map({name, price: (.price - $d)})",
    "tests": [
      {
        "input": {
          "discount": 5,
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "lamp",
              "price": 30
            },
            {
              "name": "desk",
              "price": 120
            }
          ]
        },
        "expected": "[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"lamp\",\n    \"price\": 25\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"desk\",\n    \"price\": 115\n  }\n]"
      },
      {
        "input": {
          "discount": 0,
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "chair",
              "price": 45
            }
          ]
        },
        "expected": "[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"chair\",\n    \"price\": 45\n  }\n]"
      },
      {
        "input": {
          "discount": 10,
          "items": []
        },
        "expected": "[]"
      },
      {
        "input": {
          "discount": 2,
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "mug",
              "price": 8
            },
            {
              "name": "cup",
              "price": 2
            }
          ]
        },
        "expected": "[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"mug\",\n    \"price\": 6\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cup\",\n    \"price\": 0\n  }\n]"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Names for logins",
    "statement": "Give the name of the user and the day for every login.\n\nThe `names` object maps a user id to a name. Each item of `logins` has a `user` id and a `day`. Give an array of objects with `name` and `day`. Save the names with `.names as $names`. Then `$names[.user]` reads the name for the id in `.user`.",
    "reference": ".names as $names | .logins | map({name: $names[.user], day})",
    "tests": [
      {
        "input": {
          "names": {
            "u1": "Ada",
            "u2": "Bo"
          },
          "logins": [
            {
              "user": "u2",
              "day": "Mon"
            },
            {
              "user": "u1",
              "day": "Tue"
            },
            {
              "user": "u2",
              "day": "Wed"
            }
          ]
        },
        "expected": "[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Bo\",\n    \"day\": \"Mon\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Ada\",\n    \"day\": \"Tue\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Bo\",\n    \"day\": \"Wed\"\n  }\n]"
      },
      {
        "input": {
          "names": {
            "u7": "Cy"
          },
          "logins": [
            {
              "user": "u7",
              "day": "Fri"
            }
          ]
        },
        "expected": "[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cy\",\n    \"day\": \"Fri\"\n  }\n]"
      },
      {
        "input": {
          "names": {
            "u3": "Dee",
            "u4": "Eli"
          },
          "logins": []
        },
        "expected": "[]"
      },
      {
        "input": {
          "names": {
            "a": "Fay",
            "b": "Gus",
            "c": "Hal"
          },
          "logins": [
            {
              "user": "c",
              "day": "Sat"
            },
            {
              "user": "a",
              "day": "Sun"
            }
          ]
        },
        "expected": "[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Hal\",\n    \"day\": \"Sat\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Fay\",\n    \"day\": \"Sun\"\n  }\n]"
      }
    ]
  }
]
